{% set local_problem %}
<p>Somerville's rural character means larger properties with more trees — and more debris filling gutters. Many homes here have mature pine and hardwood coverage that drops needles and leaves year-round. Traditional sectional gutters with seams every 10 feet struggle with this debris load.</p>

<p>Many Somerville homes are older properties that have been through decades of Alabama weather. Original gutters have failed, seams have separated, and fascia boards show water damage. These homes often need comprehensive replacement, not just repairs.</p>

<p>Morgan County's red clay soil makes gutter problems worse. Unlike sandy soil that absorbs water, clay forces runoff to pool and spread. When gutters overflow, that water accumulates around your foundation.</p>

<p>Seamless gutters eliminate the seam problem entirely. Custom-fabricated on-site to fit your home exactly, they have no weak points to fail.</p>
{% endset %}

{% set service_explanation %}
<p>Seamless gutters are exactly what they sound like: continuous gutters with no seams except at corners and downspout connections. Unlike traditional sectional gutters (made of pre-cut 10-foot sections joined together), seamless gutters are fabricated on-site from a single piece of aluminum coil.</p>

<p>We bring our portable gutter machine directly to your Somerville home, feed in aluminum coil, and fabricate your gutters right in your driveway. What comes out is a precision-fit gutter system designed specifically for your roofline.</p>
{% endset %}

{% set why_us %}
<p>We're based in Hartselle — another small Morgan County town. We understand that living in a small town shouldn't mean settling for second-rate service or paying extra for contractors to come out.</p>

<p>We've been serving Morgan County for over 20 years. Somerville is part of our regular territory, and we treat every home here with the same care we'd give any property in the region.</p>
{% endset %}

